---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';

const title = 'HuddleWay Privacy Policy';
const description =
  'Privacy Policy for HuddleWay Hub and HuddleWay Admin.';
---

<BaseLayout title={title} description={description} pageName="privacy-policy">
  <section class="legal-page">
    <div class="legal-page__inner">
      <p class="legal-page__eyebrow">Legal</p>
      <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
      <p class="legal-page__updated">Last updated: May 20, 2026</p>
      <p class="legal-page__lede">
        This Privacy Policy applies to HuddleWay Hub, HuddleWay Admin, and the
        related web links and backend services used to operate them.
      </p>

      <div class="legal-card">
        <h2>What HuddleWay Is</h2>
        <p>
          HuddleWay provides tools for sports programs and similar organizations
          to manage schedules, registration, payments, messaging, documents,
          branding, and family-facing updates. HuddleWay Hub is the family and
          participant-facing app. HuddleWay Admin is the operator-facing app.
        </p>

        <h2>Information We May Collect</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>Account information such as email address, account id, role, and tenant membership.</li>
          <li>Participant and family information such as names, phone numbers, addresses, ages, grades, emergency contacts, and form responses.</li>
          <li>Registration and payment records such as event selection, payment status, checkout metadata, and refund context.</li>
          <li>User content such as messages, uploads, documents, logos, photos, event images, and other files shared through the service.</li>
          <li>Device and app information such as push tokens, device platform, and app version.</li>
          <li>Diagnostics and service logs such as crash diagnostics, security logs, rate-limit records, request ids, and server log data that can include IP-address level information.</li>
          <li>Setup and link context such as QR join, invite, registration, and route handoff parameters.</li>
          <li>Optional AI-import source text and extracted setup fields when an operator chooses to use onboarding AI import.</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>How We Use Information</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>To create and secure accounts.</li>
          <li>To provide registration, scheduling, messaging, documents, and program-management workflows.</li>
          <li>To process eligible payments for real-world or off-app services.</li>
          <li>To send product messages, emails, and push notifications.</li>
          <li>To troubleshoot issues, protect the service, and investigate abuse or fraud.</li>
          <li>To support optional AI-assisted onboarding import when an operator requests it.</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>Tracking, Ads, And Sale Of Data</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>HuddleWay does not sell personal data.</li>
          <li>HuddleWay does not show ads in the iOS apps.</li>
          <li>HuddleWay does not use cross-app or cross-site tracking for this release.</li>
          <li>HuddleWay does not use App Tracking Transparency for this release.</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>Who We Share Information With</h2>
        <p>We may share information with service providers needed to operate HuddleWay, including:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Firebase and Google Cloud for authentication, database, storage, messaging, and related infrastructure.</li>
          <li>Stripe for eligible payment processing.</li>
          <li>Email-delivery providers used for communications and account workflows.</li>
          <li>OpenAI or Google AI only when an operator explicitly uses onboarding AI import.</li>
          <li>Authorities or professional advisers when needed to enforce rights, respond to abuse, or comply with law.</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>Payments</h2>
        <p>
          If a tenant enables payments, HuddleWay stores payment and checkout
          state needed for the workflow. Payment card handling is performed by
          Stripe rather than stored directly in the app code. In iOS App Store
          contexts, Stripe is intended only for real-world or off-app services.
        </p>

        <h2>Messages, Uploads, And Content</h2>
        <p>
          Operators and users may publish messages, upload documents, share
          photos, submit registrations, and exchange other content through the
          service. Operators are responsible for making sure they have the right
          to upload or distribute the content they publish.
        </p>

        <h2>Diagnostics And Notifications</h2>
        <p>
          HuddleWay may store device tokens to send notifications if
          notifications are enabled. HuddleWay may also process crash and
          diagnostic information if crash reporting is enabled for a release.
        </p>

        <h2>Retention</h2>
        <p>
          HuddleWay keeps data for as long as needed to operate the service,
          complete requested workflows, investigate abuse, satisfy accounting or
          legal obligations, and support tenant operations. Some links and
          temporary access records expire automatically. Other records may remain
          until deleted by the tenant, processed through an approved deletion
          workflow, or retained for safety, dispute, or legal reasons.
        </p>

        <h2>Account Deletion</h2>
        <p>
          Consumers may request account deletion from the Hub account screen.
          Deletion requests may require manual fulfillment. Some records may be
          retained where required for security, fraud prevention, payment,
          dispute, or legal reasons.
        </p>

        <h2>Children And Youth Data</h2>
        <p>
          HuddleWay is not presented as a Kids Category app. Some tenants may
          use it to manage youth participants, which can include participant and
          guardian data entered for program operations.
        </p>

        <h2>Contact</h2>
        <p>
          For privacy questions, support issues, or deletion follow-up, contact:
          <a href="mailto:support@huddleway.com">support@huddleway.com</a>
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
